 Helmed by his pupil's talent, Verrocchio renounced painting, and from then on did nothing but sculpture.

70
00:08:20,070 --> 00:08:23,360
 Leonardo was ashamed of the thought of hurting his beloved master.

71
00:08:23,590 --> 00:08:25,880
 None of his own sculptures would ever reach completion.

72
00:08:26,260 --> 00:08:28,200
 Was this a coincidence or a kind of self-punch?

73
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:29,400
 Three to two, huh?

74
00:08:32,640 --> 00:08:40,380
 One day, while Lorenzo de' Medici and his brother Julian were attending Mass,

75
00:08:47,380 --> 00:08:54,820
 their success, the conspirators hurried to the Lord's Palace,

76
00:08:55,040 --> 00:09:16,100
 only to find 64th's plot against the Medicis was a most miserable failure.

77
00:09:18,160 --> 00:09:20,100
 All this profoundly affected the young Leonardo,

78
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:23,330
 who finished his sketch of one of the culprits, Bernardo Bandini,

79
00:09:23,610 --> 00:09:27,390
 and then went to Santa Croce Church to study some of Giotto's work.

80
00:09:30,380 --> 00:09:34,580
 Three to two in our favor.

81
00:09:34,580 --> 00:09:44,320
 His friend Botticelli was in Rome, his beloved master Verrocchio in Venice, working on an equestrian statue of Bartolomeo Collione.

82
00:09:44,910 --> 00:09:48,090
 So he went on studying by himself in all subjects that interested him.

83
00:09:48,760 --> 00:09:58,010
 But he was so poor, he finally had to seek the patronage of the Lord of Milan, Ludivico Sforza, most noble sire.

84
00:09:58,840 --> 00:10:03,000
 After many experiments, I would like to explain some of my secrets to Your Excellency.

85
00:10:03,490 --> 00:10:06,580
 I have the means to destroy any citadel or fortress.

86
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:10,550
 I also possess all kinds of mortar, practical and portable.

87
00:10:10,950 --> 00:10:13,550
 As well as a number of weapons for naval combat.

88
00:10:14,300 --> 00:10:19,380
 I can build covered tanks, capable of penetrating enemy lines and destroying them with artillery.

89
00:10:20,040 --> 00:10:22,900
 And in peacetime, I could be most useful to you in architecture.

90
00:10:23,570 --> 00:10:27,530
 And in painting, I believe I am as capable as any other, if not more so.

91
00:10:29,360 --> 00:10:31,600
 Oh, if only I could read Plato, thought Leonardo.

92
00:10:31,900 --> 00:10:33,300
 They wouldn't treat me like a clown.

93
